Aerie-Purpose: Show the full HTTPS-only warning page, with its Continue to site button, instead of Chromium's native dialog.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: components/security_interstitials/core/features.cc (default of kHttpsFirstDialogUi)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Chromium 157 turns kHttpsFirstDialogUi on. With it the HTTPS-only fallback commits a blank
page and opens a tab-modal Views dialog. Turned off, the same fallback shows the
interstitial page ("Site is not secure") with one Continue to site button, as
docs/hardening.md promises. This is the feature default, not a command-line flag, so a
user's own field trial or --enable-features still wins.

--- a/components/security_interstitials/core/features.cc
+++ b/components/security_interstitials/core/features.cc
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 namespace security_interstitials::features {
 
 // Enables a dialog-based UI for HTTPS-First Mode.
-BASE_FEATURE(kHttpsFirstDialogUi, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+BASE_FEATURE(kHttpsFirstDialogUi, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kInsecureFormNavigationThrottleForPrerender,
              base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
